Living in a rental doesn't mean you're stuck with a cluttered bathroom. These seven storage ideas work without a single screw in the wall — and they all look intentional, not improvised.

## 1. Over-Door Organizers

The back of your bathroom door is prime real estate. A sturdy over-door rack with adjustable hooks can hold towels, hair tools, and even a small shelf for products.

**What to look for:** Choose one with rubber-coated hooks to protect the door frame — important for keeping your deposit intact.

## 2. Tension Rod Under the Sink

A tension rod stretched across the inside of your under-sink cabinet doubles your vertical storage instantly. Hang spray bottles by their triggers and suddenly you have room for a whole basket of cleaning supplies below.

## 3. Magnetic Strips for Small Items

Stick a magnetic strip (the adhesive kind) inside a cabinet door. Hair clips, bobby pins, nail scissors — everything that usually disappears into a drawer finds a home.

## 4. Freestanding Corner Shelves

No studs needed. A slim ladder shelf or corner tower in the shower area holds everything from shampoo to spare towels, and moves out with you when you leave.

## 5. Suction Cup Caddies

Modern suction caddies have come a long way — the ones with locking levers hold several pounds without budging. Great for tile walls in the shower.

## 6. Stackable Bins on the Counter

If counter space is your only option, go vertical with stackable clear bins. Keep one for daily-use items, one for extras. Easy to see, easy to grab.

## 7. Washi Tape Labels

Not a storage solution by itself, but it makes any bin system feel intentional. Washi tape peels off cleanly from most surfaces — renters' best friend.

---

**The rule of thumb:** Before buying anything, measure your door clearance, under-sink depth, and corner diagonal. Five minutes with a tape measure saves a lot of returns.
